# Local development only. These PUBLIC example credentials are not production secrets.
# Services: docker compose up -d --wait
# Tests: pnpm test:infra
# The integration tests provision the local bucket idempotently.
# Copy to .env for application development; generate a new AUTH_SECRET for deployments.
# Web/worker startup validation and deployment provisioning are wired in later M0 phases.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://sap_pm:sap-pm-local-only@127.0.0.1:55417/sap_pm
APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3017
AUTH_SECRET=local-dev-only-replace-before-deployment-32
AI_PROVIDER=stub
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# AI_PROVIDER is stub, anthropic, deepinfra (the Anthropic-compatible endpoint at api.deepinfra.com/anthropic) or openrouter (openrouter.ai/api/v1/messages).
# openrouter needs OPENROUTER_API_KEY; AI_MODEL and AI_MODEL_DESIGN default to deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 (priced 0.15 in / 0.60 out USD per MTok out of the box).
# AI_REASONING_EFFORT (openrouter only; none|low|medium|high|max, default max) is sent as output_config.effort; none sends thinking disabled.
# AI_OUTLINE_REASONING_EFFORT (openrouter, and deepinfra with a deepseek model where it is sent as thinking budget_tokens low 4000/medium 12000/high 24000/max 48000 with max_tokens raised to budget+16000 up to 64000; optional, same values) sets the effort for the to_be_outline call alone while AI_REASONING_EFFORT is unset (an explicit AI_REASONING_EFFORT wins); unset = max. Reasoning tokens count against max_tokens; none sends thinking disabled for the outline.
# AI_NO_THINKING_STAGES also applies on openrouter. OpenRouter has no count_tokens, so AI_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS is checked against a local estimate (characters / 3.5).
# deepinfra needs DEEPINFRA_API_KEY and AI_MODEL=XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash (anthropic: AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5-5).
# AI_MODEL_DESIGN (optional) is the model for the long To-Be design stage only; unset means AI_MODEL runs every stage.
# Recommended on deepinfra: AI_MODEL=XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash AI_MODEL_DESIGN=XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Pro
DEEPINFRA_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Optional credit fallback: a call the primary refuses for credit (HTTP 402) is re-sent to this provider (anthropic|deepinfra|openrouter, not AI_PROVIDER; needs its own key).
# AI_FALLBACK_MODEL / AI_FALLBACK_MODEL_DESIGN default to that provider's default model.
AI_FALLBACK_PROVIDER=
# AI_MODEL defaults to claude-sonnet-5-5; AI_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS to 60000;
# AI_MAX_CONCURRENCY (To-Be and problem analysis) to 4; AI_CHAT_CONCURRENCY (interview turns and their background extraction, own slots) to 3. The To-Be outline call (the largest) measured about 23000 tokens by chars/4, about 34000 as counted by DeepInfra MiMo, with a 65-entry catalog; the 60000 default leaves headroom.
# CONSULTANT_DAILY_JOB_LIMIT caps consultant jobs per organization per rolling 24 hours (default 200).
# AI time budgets in whole seconds (defaults shown; sized for Claude). Per-call timeouts must not exceed the stage budget.
# For a slow model such as MiMo-V2.6-Pro on DeepInfra (~12 output tokens/s measured) use:
# AI_STAGE_BUDGET_SECONDS=1200 AI_CALL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300 AI_DESIGN_CALL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=1000
# AI_STAGE_BUDGET_SECONDS=300       (60-1800) whole stage including repair attempts
# AI_CALL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120       (30-1500) one model call, ordinary stages
# AI_DESIGN_CALL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=240 (30-1500) one model call, the long To-Be design stage
# AI_DESIGN_PARALLELISM=4             (1-16) To-Be step calls in flight at once; the design is one outline call plus one call per step.
#   The whole design stage still holds a single AI_MAX_CONCURRENCY permit, so provider requests in flight can reach
#   AI_MAX_CONCURRENCY x AI_DESIGN_PARALLELISM. With MiMo (~12 tok/s per stream) use 6 or more for a 12-step design.
# AI_TO_BE_OUTLINE_REPAIRS=2          (0-2) outline repair calls after the first answer; the second only while more than half of AI_STAGE_BUDGET_SECONDS remains.
# AI_TO_BE_PART_REPAIRS=2             (0-2) re-requests per To-Be step or register call after its first answer; the second only while more than half of AI_STAGE_BUDGET_SECONDS remains.
# AI_NO_THINKING_STAGES (optional, comma-separated: problem_analysis, interview_turn, to_be, or the To-Be request kinds to_be_outline, to_be_step, to_be_registers; to_be covers all three) turns model reasoning off for those stages,
# DeepInfra and OpenRouter only (sends thinking: {type: disabled}); anthropic is refused because Claude answers 400. Recommended on deepinfra with MiMo:
# AI_NO_THINKING_STAGES=interview_turn
# AI_TO_BE_OUTLINE_MAX_TOKENS=16000 / AI_TO_BE_STEP_MAX_TOKENS=8000 / AI_TO_BE_REGISTERS_MAX_TOKENS=8000 (1000-64000) are the max_tokens of the three To-Be request kinds.
#   Reasoning tokens count against them: a thinking model needs room above the visible JSON (outline ~3k tokens, step ~3k, register group ~3.5k).
#   A call whose answer was cut off (max_tokens) or came back without a tool payload is asked again with its ceiling doubled (up to 64000) without using up a repair; each such call logs ai_output_ceiling_raised and adds the warning OUTPUT_CEILING_RAISED.
# AI_TO_BE_REVIEW=on                 (on|off, default on) after a valid design is assembled, one call (substage to_be_review) reads it whole and lists contradictions, missing links, unresolved codes and gaps;
#   each finding that names a step or register group sends that part back once, the rest become review findings. Skipped when 25% or less of AI_STAGE_BUDGET_SECONDS remains.
# AI_TO_BE_FIX_MAX_PARTS=8           (0-20, default 8, 0 = off) after the review, every fixable heuristic blocker (unmapped objective step, missing status transition, uncovered pain point, unresolved code, ...) and unresolved review finding that names a step or register group sends that part back once (substage to_be_fix, all findings for the part in one call); a repair is kept only if the design still validates and the finding no longer fires.
#   A finding that needs a step the design lacks takes one outline patch plus the new steps' calls, only while more than 40% of AI_STAGE_BUDGET_SECONDS remains (the fix pass itself: more than 25%).
# AI_TO_BE_REVIEW_ROUNDS=2          (1-3, default 2) round 1 is the review plus the fix pass; each further round reads the repaired design again and sends only its NEW findings back to the parts concerned for one more repair (parts tried in round 1 may be retried).
#   A further round only starts while the budget left exceeds what the longest round so far took (else warning REVIEW_ROUND_SKIPPED_BUDGET). 1 = the single review.
# AI_FAULT_INJECTION is off by default.
EMAIL_PROVIDER=stub
EMAIL_API_KEY=
EMAIL_FROM=sap-pm@example.test
S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:19017
S3_REGION=us-east-1
S3_BUCKET=sap-pm-local
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=sap-pm-local
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=sap-pm-local-storage-only
# Optional "Continue with Google" sign-in: set BOTH or neither (a half-set pair fails startup).
# Create an OAuth client (type: Web application) and add ${APP_URL}/api/auth/google/callback as an authorized redirect URI.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Platform admin (/admin): comma-separated sign-in emails of SaaS operators, matched case-insensitively.
# Empty or unset means nobody is a platform admin. This is separate from a workspace's ADMIN role.
PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS=
# Cost estimate on /admin, USD per million tokens. Defaults are Claude Sonnet 5.5's list price (2 input / 10 output).
# Leave unset for the defaults; adjust if the model or your contract price changes.
# AI_PRICE_INPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=2
# AI_PRICE_OUTPUT_USD_PER_MTOK=10
# AI_MODEL_PRICES (optional JSON, model id -> [input, output] USD per M tokens, each > 0 and <= 1000) prices each job by the model
# recorded in its metrics; models without an entry and older jobs use the two prices above. Recommended on deepinfra:
# AI_MODEL_PRICES={"XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Flash":[0.14,0.28],"XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Pro":[0.43,0.87]}
